<a id="ablation"></a>

## Ablation: software steps vs silicon

![ablation](../results/fig_ablation.png)

| step | type | tok/s/user | HBM busy |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for s in K.abl %}
| {{ s.id }} {{ s.step }} | {{ s.kind }} | {{ s.tok_s_user|n }} | {{ s.hbm_busy|pct }} |
{% endfor %}

Every step before A5 runs on the GPUs Baseten already has. The persistent program (A1→A2) is the
largest and least certain step: it assumes a stage hand-off can drop from the fitted
{{ cal.kernel_overhead_us|n(1) }} µs to ~1 µs, which the fit cannot confirm because κ lumps launch residue, ramp,
tail and grid-wide completion together. Flags (A2→A3) and cross-layer prefetch (A3→A4) follow.
The silicon step adds {{ sp(K.abl_by.A5.tok_s_user/K.abl_by.A4.tok_s_user - 1) }} at 4 chips.

